The dlb code has the stupid behavior of not failing when you try to
add more files to nhdat than it can manage.

It will print a warning but that warning is easily overlooked when
doing "make update" or "make install".

There's a hard coded limit of how many files are added to nhdat (in
vanilla 200, in slashem 300).

But that can be changed without a problem:
https://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/unnethack/changeset/78

